From 692da7dbd8db2ea9bd6dcbdede015a7f8842d8e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 16:37:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 017/108] core: crash context for unresolved host faults

New rex::arch fault-report API (exception_handler.h, src/core/fault_context.cpp):
SetFaultContextProvider, Begin/EndFaultDispatch and LogCurrentFaultContext,
which logs one critical block per (host PC, fault address) per thread: reason,
host PC, fault address, provider lines and a symbolised host backtrace (up to
24 frames), then flushes the logs.

- Windows: unwinds from the faulting CONTEXT (RtlLookupFunctionEntry /
  RtlVirtualUnwind; RtlCaptureStackBackTrace fallback) and symbolises with
  dbghelp loaded at runtime (module!symbol+off, or module+off without PDB).
  A chained SetUnhandledExceptionFilter reports truly unhandled exceptions and
  then defers to the previous filter, so the process dies as before.
- POSIX/Android: _Unwind_Backtrace + dladdr (+ demangling); the signal handler
  reports when no installed handler resolved the fault, behaviour after that
  is unchanged.
- The VEH/signal handlers only record (pc, address, context) in a
  thread_local before running handlers: no cost unless a fault goes unhandled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/include/rex/exception_handler.h b/include/rex/exception_handler.h
index bcd00bf..9a16172 100644
--- a/include/rex/exception_handler.h
+++ b/include/rex/exception_handler.h
@@ -531,4 +531,26 @@ class ExceptionHandler {
   static void Uninstall(Handler fn, void* data);
 };
 
+//=============================================================================
+// Fault crash context (cold path: only used once a fault is not resolved)
+//=============================================================================
+
+// Optional extra lines for the fault report (e.g. guest thread name/entry).
+// Set by the runtime; called on the faulting thread. Appends to `out`.
+using FaultContextProvider = void (*)(std::string& out);
+void SetFaultContextProvider(FaultContextProvider provider);
+
+// Records the fault being dispatched on this thread (called by the platform
+// exception handlers before running the installed handlers; `platform_context`
+// is EXCEPTION_POINTERS* on Windows, ucontext_t* on POSIX).
+void BeginFaultDispatch(uint64_t host_pc, uint64_t fault_address, const void* platform_context);
+void EndFaultDispatch();
+
+// Logs one critical block for the fault currently being dispatched on this
+// thread: reason, host PC, fault address, guest context (provider) and a
+// symbolised host backtrace (up to 24 frames), then flushes the logs. Logs at
+// most once per (host PC, fault address) per thread; no-op outside a fault.
+// Never resolves the fault: callers keep their normal failure path.
+void LogCurrentFaultContext(const char* reason);
+
 }  // namespace rex::arch
